==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|assimulatus|assimulātus|made similar, imitated|lang=la}}, perfect passive participle of {{term|assimulo|assimulō|lang=la}}, from {{term|ad|lang=la}} + {{term|simulo|simulō|imitate, copy|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US}} {{IPA|/əˈsɪm.ɪ.leɪt/}}
* {{audio|en-us-assimilate.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|assimilat|ing}}

# To [[incorporate]] [[nutrient]]s into the [[body]] after [[digestion]].
# To incorporate or [[absorb]] [[knowledge]] into the [[mind]].
#: ''The teacher paused in her lecture to allow the students to '''assimilate''' what she had said.''
# To absorb a group of [[people]] into a [[community]].
# To [[compare]] something to another [[similar]] one.

